WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
A wheel sits at rest on a smooth axle.

2
00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.350
A motor starts to turn it.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.050
Its twist is strong at
first, then weakens steadily,

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.680
fading to nothing.

5
00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.510
For a steady twist,
there are simple rules:

6
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.980
twist times angle turned,
or twist times time.

7
00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.730
But this twist changes all the time.

8
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:25.700
When a twist keeps changing, how do you
find the spin and the energy it gives?

9
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.590
In this mission, you'll
treat spin as a vector,

10
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.390
with a direction set by your right hand.

11
00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.400
Then you'll follow a wheel
as the twist on it fades,

12
00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.070
and find how fast it ends up spinning.

13
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:41.950
Your mission: work out the spin and
the energy that a changing twist gives.
